    "['encapsulation flexible-ethernet-services', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n portswitch\\n port link-type hybrid\\n port hybrid tagged vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command enables flexible Ethernet services on the interface, which is similar to creating a hybrid/L2 interface in Huawei that can handle VLAN tagging.\\n- In Huawei, we use `portswitch` to switch the interface to L2 mode.\\n- `port link-type hybrid` allows the interface to process both tagged and untagged traffic.\\n- The VLAN 10 is specified since it's referenced in the subsequent Juniper configuration (unit 10 with vlan-id 10).\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'portswitch', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n portswitch\\n port link-type hybrid\\n port hybrid tagged vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command enables flexible Ethernet services on the interface, which is similar to creating a hybrid/L2 interface in Huawei that can handle VLAN tagging.\\n- In Huawei, we use `portswitch` to switch the interface to L2 mode.\\n- `port link-type hybrid` allows the interface to process both tagged and untagged traffic.\\n- The VLAN 10 is specified since it's referenced in the subsequent Juniper configuration (unit 10 with vlan-id 10).\", 'trans_template': 'portswitch'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port link-type hybrid', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n portswitch\\n port link-type hybrid\\n port hybrid tagged vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command enables flexible Ethernet services on the interface, which is similar to creating a hybrid/L2 interface in Huawei that can handle VLAN tagging.\\n- In Huawei, we use `portswitch` to switch the interface to L2 mode.\\n- `port link-type hybrid` allows the interface to process both tagged and untagged traffic.\\n- The VLAN 10 is specified since it's referenced in the subsequent Juniper configuration (unit 10 with vlan-id 10).\", 'trans_template': 'port link-type hybrid'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'port hybrid tagged vlan 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n portswitch\\n port link-type hybrid\\n port hybrid tagged vlan 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command enables flexible Ethernet services on the interface, which is similar to creating a hybrid/L2 interface in Huawei that can handle VLAN tagging.\\n- In Huawei, we use `portswitch` to switch the interface to L2 mode.\\n- `port link-type hybrid` allows the interface to process both tagged and untagged traffic.\\n- The VLAN 10 is specified since it's referenced in the subsequent Juniper configuration (unit 10 with vlan-id 10).\", 'trans_template': 'port hybrid tagged vlan 10'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit-number] encapsulation [encapsulation-type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.10 dot1q termination vid 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated command for HUAWEI router:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.10 dot1q termination vid 10\\nbridge-domain 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command sets unit 10 with VLAN bridging encapsulation for VLAN 10\\n- In HUAWEI:\\n  - `dot1q termination vid 10` creates the sub-interface with VLAN 10 tagging\\n  - `bridge-domain 10` places the sub-interface in a bridge domain (equivalent to Juniper's vlan-bridge encapsulation)\\n- Note that HUAWEI requires these as separate commands to achieve the same effect as Juniper's single command\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.10 dot1q termination vid 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'bridge-domain 10', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated command for HUAWEI router:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.10 dot1q termination vid 10\\nbridge-domain 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command sets unit 10 with VLAN bridging encapsulation for VLAN 10\\n- In HUAWEI:\\n  - `dot1q termination vid 10` creates the sub-interface with VLAN 10 tagging\\n  - `bridge-domain 10` places the sub-interface in a bridge domain (equivalent to Juniper's vlan-bridge encapsulation)\\n- Note that HUAWEI requires these as separate commands to achieve the same effect as Juniper's single command\", 'trans_template': 'bridge-domain 10'}]]": 1,
